{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#4142","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#4142","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#4142\",\"parent_revision\":\"78561f72ec684140c03bde776d7217b298b421e714d7a3c43195b382d48ecbae\",\"root_revision\":\"78561f72ec684140c03bde776d7217b298b421e714d7a3c43195b382d48ecbae\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: needs-grooming\\nadded: 2026-10-17\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-10-17T07:20:34.732459Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: feat: itsaplan as a WorkItemBackend provider over its REST API and MCP endpoint\\nDate: 2026-10-17\\nGoal: Establish whether Itsaplan can serve as the configured DH work-item provider while preserving the provider-neutral ownership and lifecycle contract.\\nConditions:\\n1. DH work-item lifecycle, identity, status, milestone, capability, and remote-provider ownership requirements are documented in source. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Itsaplan work-item endpoints, identity format, list pagination, and authenticated permissions can be verified from its current OpenAPI/API source. | Status: DERIVABLE\\n3. Itsaplan support for DH logical plan and artifact content records, revision/conflict behavior, and bounded discovery can be verified from its current API source. | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. The target deployment URL, supported Itsaplan version, credential provisioning and permission scope are selected for a future implementation. | Status: MISSING\\n5. A native milestone capability matching DHs numeric milestone contract is verified, or a human-approved unsupported behavior is recorded. | Status: DERIVABLE\\n6. Backend provider work is scoped independently from Itsaplan runner integration in #4143. | Status: AVAILABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 1\\nDecision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n</div>\\n\\n## Offers\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nresearch/task-management/itsaplan.md, \\\"Key Features > Platform\\\" and \\\"Problem Addressed\\\": a self-hosted tracker exposing a REST API with an OpenAPI reference and API keys, and an MCP endpoint at `POST /mcp` (Bearer or `x-api-key` auth). The entry states: \\\"REST API with an OpenAPI reference and API keys.\\\" and \\\"MCP endpoint at `POST /mcp`.\\\" It also documents an extension point: \\\"any API route can be exposed by adding an `x-mcp` extension to its OpenAPI detail\\\" (entry, Technical Architecture, Extension points).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Touches\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe dh backlog backend contract. `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_types.py:182` defines `class WorkItemBackend(Protocol)`, documented as \\\"Generic work-item surface every backend must implement\\\". `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py:176` sets `_VALID_BACKENDS: tuple[str, ...] = (\\\"github\\\", \\\"memory\\\", \\\"sqlite\\\", \\\"beads\\\")`. The factory `create_backend` at `backend_protocol.py:179` dispatches on that name.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Could Change\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new backend family, `itsaplan`, implementing `WorkItemBackend` over the itsaplan REST API or its MCP endpoint, so that the dh backlog MCP server reads and writes work items in a self-hosted tracker instead of GitHub Issues. Setup cost: a running itsaplan instance (entry, Installation: Docker and Bun, PostgreSQL, api/worker/web services), an API key, and a `create_backend` branch plus a `_VALID_BACKENDS` entry. `WorkItemBackend` requires milestone create, list and assign methods on every backend; `backend_types.py:199-207` documents the `supports_milestones` flag and the `NotImplementedError` escape hatch. The entry lists no milestone concept among its features, so mapping milestones is a required check before implementation.\\n\\nRelated open issues, not duplicates: #1177 (formalise an adapter Protocol for GitLab and Linear), #3262 (WorkItemBackend method names are GitHub-specific).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Read: `research/task-management/itsaplan.md` lines 36-64 (Platform list) and 92-96 (Extension points).\\n- Read: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_types.py` lines 175-214.\\n- Read: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` lines 170-182.\\n- Grep `backend\\\\.name|_VALID_BACKENDS|class \\\\w+(Backend|Provider)` in `plugins/development-harness`: `_VALID_BACKENDS` is the only tuple of backend family names.\\n- GitHub issue search `repo:Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills itsaplan`: 0 results.\\n- GitHub issue search `repo:Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills backend tracker Linear GitLab new backend WorkItemBackend`: #1177, #3262.\\n- Filing route: backlog MCP `backlog_add` failed (see ROUTE_FAILURES); filed through GitHub MCP `issue_write`.\\n- Semantic search tools (ccc, graphify) were not run in this scan. Grep and Glob were the search tools used.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a7bb3867cc880fdba823bbb7d63e3c70d28fc2dfaa12a86f05419a1f945fffe0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABc2fANw\",\"fields\":{\"topic\":\"\",\"plan\":\"\",\"priority\":\"P2\",\"stack\":\"\",\"close_reference\":\"\",\"status\":\"needs-grooming\",\"close_comment\":\"\",\"source\":\"Not specified\",\"added\":\"2026-10-17\",\"suggested_location\":\"\",\"followup_to\":\"\",\"language\":\"\",\"groomed\":\"2026-10-17\",\"item_type\":\"Feature\",\"close_reason\":\"\",\"layer\":\"\",\"research_first\":\"\",\"files\":\"\"}}"}